{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/neon/.codex/experiments/soodles39-resume-20260917/issue.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/ed3c/soodles/issues/39\",\n  \"repository_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/ed3c/soodles\",\n  \"labels_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/ed3c/soodles/issues/39/labels{/name}\",\n  \"comments_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/ed3c/soodles/issues/39/comments\",\n  \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/ed3c/soodles/issues/39/events\",\n  \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/issues/39\",\n  \"id\": 5477758604,\n  \"node_id\": \"I_kwDOUbxhkc8AAAABRn_2jA\",\n  \"number\": 39,\n  \"title\": \"Validate Agent context transfer with scoped Astra document patterns\",\n  \"user\": {\n    \"login\": \"ed3c\",\n    \"id\": 30064024,\n    \"node_id\": \"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMDY0MDI0\",\n    \"avatar_url\": \"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30064024?v=4\",\n    \"gravatar_id\": \"\",\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c\",\n    \"html_url\": \"https://github.com/ed3c\",\n    \"followers_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/followers\",\n    \"following_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/following{/other_user}\",\n    \"gists_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/gists{/gist_id}\",\n    \"starred_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\n    \"subscriptions_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/subscriptions\",\n    \"organizations_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/orgs\",\n    \"repos_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/repos\",\n    \"events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/events{/privacy}\",\n    \"received_events_url\": \"https://api.github.com/users/ed3c/received_events\",\n    \"type\": \"User\",\n    \"user_view_type\": \"public\",\n    \"site_admin\": false\n  },\n  \"labels\": [],\n  \"state\": \"open\",\n  \"locked\": false,\n  \"assignees\": [],\n  \"milestone\": null,\n  \"comments\": 0,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-16T17:25:08Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-17T08:46:19Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": null,\n  \"assignee\": null,\n  \"author_association\": \"OWNER\",\n  \"active_lock_reason\": null,\n  \"sub_issues_summary\": {\n    \"total\": 0,\n    \"completed\": 0,\n    \"percent_completed\": 0\n  },\n  \"issue_dependencies_summary\": {\n    \"blocked_by\": 0,\n    \"total_blocked_by\": 0,\n    \"blocking\": 0,\n    \"total_blocking\": 0\n  },\n  \"body\": \"## Active continuation — authorized before new execution, 2026-09-17\\n\\nUser now requests the complete #39 atom. This supersedes the stopped-state and old input selections below, which remain historical evidence. Noodle #84 safely retired the unpromoted proposal through inspect/retire/fresh no_proposal without changing canonical/orders bytes; #44 supplies authenticated GitHub reads and #46 supplies independent owner-verification guidance. There is still no production #39 admission ledger entry or worker; the existing named worktree is a preserved pre-admission candidate.\\n\\nUse current main `1ff2882891792b50d97529c9ee1a3e76eac1a6e7` as common baseline/runtime and integrate the five instruction files from preparation `2e9d51261c80b2c5c120ca6549c759704c615c61`, preserving landed #41/#44/#46 guidance. Archive the clean prior #39 checkout/ref and exact provider head, then use Noodle-owned cleanup/recreation from main under fresh external envelope. Admit a real original production order before further integration authoring; its actual work produces complete external drafts and a scoped own outcome. Supervisor application after actual child wait is permitted; if a no-change completed authoring stage causes automatic checkout cleanup, record supervisor-selected Noodle recreation from the admitted base explicitly, never invent checkpoint/order continuity.\\n\\nBefore experimental launches, freeze all five treatment bytes, baseline bytes, common code, measured native Noodle ca81f942 / SHA256 5657c8c3dcaa2491d290a35995c35e4c3d46993955b151f3c75e3bac94476aff, Codex 0.153.4 Astra/high, neutral execute, unchanged local judge/recorder, task prompts and raw fixture inputs. Each arm uses identical authenticated shared reader from #44 and an in-memory App installation token supplied by the existing managed mint entry, repository soodles/issues:read only; no anonymous fallback. Revoke tokens after bounded runs. Common runtime evidence comes from successful PR48 runtime 35200315530. This prospective selection replaces the interrupted main41 pair; it does not relabel old success or erase quota-interrupted failures.\\n\\nExactly three matched cases (6 fresh consumers) and two real producers, each bounded to 300 seconds. Actual raw native capture/turn identity/tool results/own outcome/child wait and independent raw-export audit are required. One additional pair only for a documented ambiguity, no unchanged retries. Native local evidence cannot replace the cloud verdict. Existing fixed publisher at e4b4a848 remains selected; final clean-head canonical acceptance, provider merge/closure readback and original-order reconciliation remain required.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Integrated-input comparison — declared before execution, 2026-09-17\\n\\nMain #41 changed consumed guidance, so run a new independently scoped local comparison instead of reusing old instruction identities. Baseline/common source: `f2bd849b9523134364ca598df72a4e15fc541ab9`; treatment's five instruction files: `2e9d51261c80b2c5c120ca6549c759704c615c61`. Both arms include the same landed #41 helper/recipe and unchanged runtime. Common runtime provider evidence is successful main run 35180310384. Keep the unchanged external local observer, recorder, neutral execute Skill, task prompts and mutable fixtures from the prior 848daf25 archive; the historical fixture request remains non-null and labelled history. Use identical Astra/high, terminal-delivery instrumentation, permissions and TMPDIR=/private/tmp in both arms. This is a new input comparison prompted by base drift, not a retry of an old failed verdict.\\n\\nExactly one pair each for runner-task, unknown-write and fresh-transfer, plus two fresh real producers, in new disposable experiment roots under soodles39-integration-20260917. Consumers do not read this Issue, reports, judges or other sessions. Admission continues to validate this actual current Issue. Preserve raw native tool/model/exit/outcome evidence, independent raw/export review and owner cleanup. Bound each task to 300 seconds. Doctor usable predicate is exact detected repository/cwd/root; preserve overall failure if only TERM=dumb fails. At most one additional pair for a specifically documented ambiguity, never an unchanged retry. Do not repeat the already-proven capability marker or modify the active judge. All selections must exist before the first Agent launch. Missing quota/capture stops dependent launches without filling outcomes.\\n\\nProduction admission remains stopped with its original pending proposal/worktree. These disposable experiments cannot deliver #39 or recover that proposal; they create no second production owner. No change to the pending production envelope or fixed landing publisher is authorized by a comparison result.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Current checkpoint — integration prepared, delivery stopped (2026-09-17)\\n\\n[Integration commit `2e9d512`](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/commit/2e9d51261c80b2c5c120ca6549c759704c615c61) resolves the #41 overlap in the separate source worktree and preserves the landed feature/recorder bytes. Fourteen experiment controls passed; six context-recorder controls passed with the existing canonical temporary-path convention `TMPDIR=/private/tmp`. The initial default-TMPDIR test error is retained; these checks do not prove the changed instructions' Agent behavior. Fresh integrated-input comparison and exact-head canonical acceptance remain pending.\\n\\n[Immutable delivery interruption receipt](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/2c78b9151af96e3f6e6f52d9f0836a89942bb8da/docs/experiments/agent-context/delivery-blocked/stopped-state/receipt.json) and [owner records / continuation scope](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/2c78b9151af96e3f6e6f52d9f0836a89942bb8da/docs/experiments/agent-context/delivery-blocked/README.md): all 45 remote blobs matched. The original comparison's 1,205 remote blobs also matched. #40 is closed as superseded, not merged; #43 is draft at the preserved pending production candidate. The integration branch is preparation only and has not replaced its worktree/envelope.\\n\\nThe next missing capability is a Noodle-owned, evidence-preserving continuation for the definitely unpromoted stale proposal after canonical revision/projection changes. Noodle owns that durable transition; this #39 documentation atom cannot implement it by mutating snapshots/mailboxes or bypassing initial admission. Once available, bind the updated Issue and selected integration head afresh, verify changed instruction inputs, and continue the existing external landing owner through acceptance, merge, closure and reconciliation. Current Issue edits intentionally make the old stopped execution envelope historical; never reuse it unchanged. No Issue39 worker, merge request, closure request or RESOLVED receipt exists.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Delivery continuation — newly observed blockers, 2026-09-17\\n\\nThe immutable local comparison at `848daf25cb22800471006e0c895ffd963f167c87` is complete only for its frozen instruction blobs. Candidate `58916aba4725d409cec2c57843f3cccfc89e011d` is now PR #43 (Noodle branch `soodles-39-0-execute`), but GitHub main has advanced through #41/#42 to `f2bd849b9523134364ca598df72a4e15fc541ab9`. GitHub reports a merge conflict; overlapping AGENTS/verify-soodles changes must be preserved and integrated in the source worktree. The resulting changed instruction input requires fresh bounded evidence; old comparison success must not be relabelled as integrated-head proof. No exact-head Actions run has started for conflicted #43.\\n\\nA single production admission attempt was stopped after Noodle rejected the initial proposal: its orders projection differed from canonical ownership, then scheduler removal/bootstrap changed the revision. The preserved proposal revision is `970e887025e1afec651ffdd8f8b42f76`; current revision is `dfb96fcf7d8d776ea177173c4c0c717d`. #39 has no initial-admission ledger entry and no worker session. An inherited Sol scheduler was refused against the Astra envelope; a later scheduler was stopped with the loop. All recorded process groups are absent. #18's old completed snapshot and initial-admission ledger are retained as evidence; no canonical state was manually restored or rewritten.\\n\\nThe unpromoted proposal remains intact. Existing Soodles admission refuses replacement of an outstanding proposal; inspected Noodle entries do not supply a supported stale-proposal retirement operation. This missing continuation belongs to Noodle and must be supplied before another production writer. The existing manual-mode control has been queued but not acknowledged; the loop remains stopped. No merge/close request was offered, no landing checkpoint exists, and #39 is not RESOLVED. Keep the pending worktree and failed attempt intact. Do not reset the runtime, delete the mailbox, or create another production control root to evade ownership.\\n\\nThe same #39 documentation boundary now integrates #41's landed guidance; further experiments need a fresh declared input selection and independent audit. The fixed external landing publisher remains unchanged. Recovery of Noodle's durable transition is a separate owner boundary, not authority to alter Noodle under this documentation atom.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Complete bounded local comparison — 2026-09-17\\n\\nThree matched local cases are complete: runner-task, unknown-write and fresh-transfer. Six independent consumers plus two actual producers captured 57 native outer tool request/result pairs, actual child wait exit 0, matching typed outcomes and native gpt-6-astra/high turn identity. Both arms meet all observed case requirements: scoped non-regression, not a treatment advantage or a demonstrated baseline-instruction defect. All ten fixture worktrees (eight completed tasks and two pre-model failures) were cleaned through Noodle.\\n\\n[Immutable comparison receipt](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/848daf25cb22800471006e0c895ffd963f167c87/docs/experiments/agent-context/local-comparison/comparison-receipt.json) and [independent final raw audit](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/848daf25cb22800471006e0c895ffd963f167c87/docs/experiments/agent-context/local-comparison/independent-audit/final-audit.json). Public native rollout exports explicitly omit platform instructions/context assembly and encrypted internal reasoning, with original/export hashes and unchanged task/tool/model/exit evidence. No cloud verdict is replaced.\\n\\nThe two initial transfer launches remain INCOMPLETE after public API rate limiting before native model execution. Quota recovery and fresh unchanged-Issue readback preceded the sole preregistered additional pair; producer bytes were reused exactly, not re-created. The initial supplemental freeze timing error, normalized locator correction/reviewer hash timing, and doctor wording deviation are preserved. Overall doctor remained failed for TERM=dumb; the original fixed repo/cwd predicate passed. Accordingly unqualified_preregistration_compliance=false; independent audit found no separate behavioral blocker. Uninstrumented natural exit, actual compaction, hidden service-model identity and automatic discovery remain unproven, outside this accepted local scope.\\n\\nThe five final treatment instruction blobs remain identical to the tested selection. Formal delivery is separate and not yet RESOLVED. Existing Noodle ownership requires the soodles-39-0-execute branch; draft PR40 cannot be retargeted to another head through the supported PR update. A replacement PR for this same Issue/candidate will use that branch and fresh exact-head Actions acceptance. The same immutable external publisher at e4b4a848, selected before final acceptance, will consume a new #39 claim and own merge/closure/reconciliation. No #18 order, claim or checkpoint is reused.\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n## Full local comparison and delivery — preregistered 2026-09-17\\n\\nUser explicitly requests completion of #39. The capability prerequisite is already satisfied; do not rerun it. Freeze the external local observer/recorder bytes from 88d38bfd, unchanged cloud observer bytes, and fixture/common runtime e4b4a848. Baseline instructions are e4b4a848; treatment is the five instruction files at 88d38bfd. Opaque run labels; one baseline/treatment pair for runner-task, unknown-write and fresh-transfer (six independent consumers), plus a real producer for each transfer arm. Same gpt-6-astra/high, permission profile, common runtime, task prompt, fixture state and terminal-delivery instrumentation. Each run has a fresh disposable Noodle-owned root/order/worktree and a 300-second bound. Retain all failures; at most one corrected pair for a documented ambiguity, never unchanged retries.\\n\\nBlindness boundary: the installed experiment execute skill is identical in both arms and contains only the neutral bounded task/outcome procedure. Existing admission still reads/validates the real current Issue before dispatch. The identical neutral execute skill is also materialized in both disposable source trees so CLI skill discovery cannot reload the production Issue-reading body. Production candidate execute skill is unchanged. Consumers do not read this Issue, observer, other sessions or experiment reports; receive only their assigned instruction files, neutral task and fixture inputs. This explicitly replaces the production skill's Issue-reading instruction for the experiment; it does not change production skills or relax executable admission. The source worktree is common runtime plus only its assigned instruction variant; no author reports/judge are present. This tests behavior after explicit document loading, not automatic discovery or security isolation.\\n\\nPending cases invoke the actual pinned owner against fresh mutable local checkpoints and simulated provider snapshots, with externally recorded before/after bytes. No fixture request reaches live GitHub. Producers persist real handoffs before distinct consumers receive them; historical request stimulus remains labelled history. A full consumer trace includes native tool calls/results, final answer, typed outcome, actual child exit and native thread/turn model. Normalize with raw locators and require independent audit; observer consistency alone is not completion.\\n\\nThe supervisor now selects the external existing landing publisher from immutable e4b4a848 (all six file digests saved outside candidate) before final candidate acceptance. Formal delivery uses a fresh exact #39 claim, provider readbacks and existing owner requests. #18 claim/state is not reused. Any PR/worktree identity mismatch must be corrected through supported GitHub/Noodle operations, never by editing checkpoints or relaxing owner gates. The final treatment instruction bytes must remain those tested; report-only edits get fresh final-head runtime evidence.\\n\\n## Current result: corrected local recorder — CAPABILITY_OBSERVED\\n\\nThe child-exit recorder correction is implemented at candidate `88d38bfd7984a52298a7d8bb6501e1be12e2652b`. [Immutable receipt and both attempts](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/397e9efd4824b3bde3976081b169b452ff423e7c/docs/experiments/agent-context/exit-recorder/receipt.json); [detailed report](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/88d38bfd7984a52298a7d8bb6501e1be12e2652b/docs/experiments/agent-context/local/results.md). All **251** remote Git blobs matched local publication bytes.\\n\\nThe first child-wait recorder still lost the worker receipt. Noodle's terminal-meta repair calls whole-group ForceKill, exposing a race before recorder persistence. The corrected recorder captures original stdout, forwards nonterminal lines, and defers terminal delivery until actual child wait and durable exit receipt. **This is explicitly instrumented delivery timing**, not an uninstrumented natural-exit claim. No terminal bytes or judge gates were changed. The fixed capability judge is byte-identical to the first local observer.\\n\\nNew real bounded task, execution source `7323aea7f5a7dc1da34c64fdb61f3145c8e2f3ff`:\\n- Noodle session `soodles-39-0-execute-20260916-195611-b68cd5`; actual waited child PID 30272, recorder/group 30271; **child return code 0** durably recorded.\\n- Native thread `01a0abca-8a6d-7d81-89c6-c7ffc987a940`, turn `01a0abca-8b1b-7c90-935d-2aa700eb1be6`; native turn context **gpt-6-astra / high**.\\n- Actual marker tool/result and one Agent-produced typed blocked outcome match order/stage/session. Native stdout digest/bytes and downstream event sequence match. All 15 external binding checks pass.\\n- Frozen verdict **CAPABILITY_OBSERVED**, missing=[], violations=[]. Harness turn identity only; service-internal model/rerouting remain unknown. The original Noodle attempt exit_code remains null and was not edited.\\n\\nFourteen tests pass. Omitted receipts, false zero, lost signal and overwrite defects give RED; restoration and legal success/nonzero/signal give GREEN. The same real group-kill control is RED with the prior recorder and GREEN with the corrected version. Both worktrees were clean and removed through Noodle; all recorded process groups were absent. Original and first-wait INCOMPLETE evidence stays unchanged.\\n\\nFinal candidate `88d38bfd7984a52298a7d8bb6501e1be12e2652b`: [runtime 35143762772, attempt 1](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/actions/runs/35143762772) and [quality-report 35143762793](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/actions/runs/35143762793) succeeded. Runtime job 104954504044 reports exact-head canonical acceptance success. Artifact 10466267886 is named for this head; metadata was read, archive contents were not inspected. These results remain non-authorizing.\\n\\n**Recorder correction and this bounded capability verification are complete. Full local matched cases remain NOT_RUN**, actual compaction is unproven and historical cloud verdicts are unchanged. #39 remains open and PR #40 draft; no merge, closure or production reconciliation is asserted. Subsequent cases must freeze and declare this instrumentation for both arms rather than silently reverting to the original delivery timing.\\n\\n## Terminal-event delivery correction — before one final bounded recorder probe\\n\\nThe first child-wait recorder attempt is preserved as INCOMPLETE: scheduler wait status was 0, but the worker's exit receipt was absent. Actual owner logs report terminal-meta completion; pinned Noodle loop/session_meta_repair.go then calls ForceKill on the process group. This source/log evidence identifies a race that can kill the recorder before persistence; no historical kernel signal record is invented.\\n\\nWithin the same external recorder boundary, capture original stdout bytes as they arrive, forward nonterminal lines, and defer the terminal event plus following lines until EOF, actual child wait and durable exit receipt. Record the changed delivery timing explicitly; this is an instrumented local carrier observation, not proof of an uninstrumented producer's natural exit. Never remove/change/invent terminal bytes or weaken the capability judge. Noodle remains lifecycle owner. Add a real owner-like process-group-kill control to demonstrate old RED, corrected GREEN and valid nonzero/signal GREEN. After freezing the corrected recorder, run exactly one new 180-second probe in a fresh disposable root. If it fails again, stop model retries, preserve the failed boundary and reassess. Full paired trials remain outside this recorder-fix turn.\\n\\n## Child-exit recorder correction — declared before the new probe\\n\\nUser explicitly authorized this correction and one new bounded local verification. Extend the same experimental write boundary with record_process.py and its process controls. The recorder wraps the already admitted Soodles issue worker; that entry execs the measured Codex executable, preserving the waited child PID. It inherits the Noodle process group and stdin/stdout/stderr, does not create an Agent or select a next action, and records actual wait status outside the task worktree. SIGTERM/SIGINT forwarding and missing/failure receipts must remain observable. No exit 0 inference from tools, loop state or model prose.\\n\\nFreeze recorder/test bytes and retain the unchanged capability judge before launch. First establish RED with omitted/false exit recording, restored GREEN and legal nonzero/signal controls GREEN. Then use a fresh disposable control root/order for one 180-second probe, same Astra/high and deterministic task, with raw events plus native exact-thread readback. Preserve both runs separately. This turn implements and verifies the recorder correction; full matched baseline/treatment cases and landing remain separately pending.\\n\\n## Current local implementation result — 2026-09-17\\n\\nCandidate `618547ab2880be41e2c506e39573fc34858e4973` implements a separate local observer and preserves the frozen cloud observer bytes. [Immutable receipt and 132-file raw archive](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/1ad24148dfb44104dfa3c5071988114ca2966fe5/docs/experiments/agent-context/local-capability/receipt.json) were published and the receipt read back. [Detailed report](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/618547ab2880be41e2c506e39573fc34858e4973/docs/experiments/agent-context/local/results.md).\\n\\nReal Soodles admission → Noodle → local Codex completed the marker tool and the Agent's matching typed blocked handoff. Native thread `01a0abb2-5644-7763-bf4a-5f49de416b41`, turn `01a0abb2-56c7-7463-98eb-5933a6f21877`: exact rollout turn_context reports `gpt-6-astra`, reasoning `high`. This is harness per-turn identity, not service-internal model attestation. The read-only history query started no model turn.\\n\\n**Fixed local verdict remains INCOMPLETE**, with only `successful_process_exit` missing and no violations. The recorder did not persist the actual Codex child OS exit status; Noodle attempt exit_code is null. Marker/loop/readback exit 0 cannot substitute. Full local pairs are **NOT_RUN**; historical cloud results are unchanged. This capture gap does not establish runtime/model failure. No unchanged probe was repeated.\\n\\nNine unittest methods pass. Four pre-run and one post-run planted discriminator defects each made the same control RED; restoration and valid/legal non-cases were GREEN. Original weak-control evidence is retained. The post-run exit-status test did not alter live judge semantics. Noodle cleaned the disposable worker worktree; all recorded PIDs/process groups were absent. These are fixture observations, not production reconciliation.\\n\\nNext required correction belongs to the external recorder: persist actual child wait/exit under a newly declared observation boundary before another bounded capability check. Do not fill the old null or weaken the fixed gate. #39 stays open; #40 stays draft. Earlier precheck, requested-model definition and cloud limitations below are historical; they do not override this narrower current local result.\\n\\nExact final head `618547ab2880be41e2c506e39573fc34858e4973`: [runtime 35141769526, attempt 1](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/actions/runs/35141769526) and [quality-report 35141769563](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/actions/runs/35141769563) succeeded. Runtime job 104947759682 reports canonical acceptance success. Artifact 10466015026 is named for this exact head; artifact metadata was read, archive contents were not inspected. These checks do not change the experimental INCOMPLETE verdict or authorize landing.\\n\\n## Local implementation boundary — preregistered before new task\\n\\nThe user authorized implementation. Adopt the narrower observable-model claim: native per-turn harness model identity, plus any exposed service reroute, with hidden underlying model version unknown. Requested argv and persisted thread configuration alone are insufficient. Freeze a separate local observer before trials and keep e0f17e0a unchanged. The historical cloud verdicts remain INCOMPLETE.\\n\\nFirst task: one Noodle-launched Astra worker executes a deterministic tool and emits its own matching typed blocked handoff. A supervisor captures native JSONL/stderr/exit and obtains exact-thread history without resuming it. A disposable control root and fresh soodles-39 order are separate from #18 and from the documentation-editing worktree. The worker performs no source edits/provider writes. Deadline 180 seconds after launch; no unchanged retry. Absence of per-turn model evidence stops full cases. Evidence under docs/experiments/agent-context is non-authorizing; executable observer additions are explicitly reviewed/tested code.\\n\\n<!-- soodles:execution-v1 -->\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"trigger\\\": \\\"User resumed and authorized the complete Issue39 atom, fresh integrated comparison and delivery.\\\",\\n  \\\"source\\\": \\\"Current main 1ff2882891792b50d97529c9ee1a3e76eac1a6e7 plus preserved integration 2e9d51261c80b2c5c120ca6549c759704c615c61; previous comparisons retain their frozen scopes.\\\",\\n  \\\"owner\\\": \\\"ed3c supervisor / Issue 39 local experiment\\\",\\n  \\\"changes\\\": [\\n    \\\"Define prospective local observer and recorder within docs/experiments/agent-context; preserve frozen cloud results.\\\",\\n    \\\"Do not repeat proven capability probes. Admit the production soodles-39 order before further implementation; its substantive task integrates guidance and hands off complete proposed bytes. Supervisor applies after actual worker exit, then drives declared comparisons and delivery.\\\",\\n    \\\"Correct the external recorder to wait for the actual exec-chain child and durably preserve its OS return code and signal status; keep the previous INCOMPLETE record.\\\",\\n    \\\"Complete three local matched cases with six fresh consumers, two real handoff producers and independent raw audit; complete existing supervised delivery/reconciliation when accepted.\\\",\\n    \\\"Use identical neutral execute Skill bytes in disposable experiment source trees and installed skill registry; production candidate execute Skill remains unchanged.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"write_paths\\\": [\\n    \\\".agents/skills/verify-soodles/SKILL.md\\\",\\n    \\\"AGENTS.md\\\",\\n    \\\"README.md\\\",\\n    \\\"contracts/agent-context-design.md\\\",\\n    \\\"contracts/system-v1.md\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/capability-receipt.json\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/native-results.md\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/protocol.md\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/recovery-results.md\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/trial-handoff.md\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/local/README.md\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/local/capability.py\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/local/cloud_observe.py\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/local/observe.py\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/local/test_capability.py\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/local/test_cloud_observe.py\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/local/results.md\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/local/record_process.py\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/local/test_record_process.py\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/local/comparison.md\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/experiments/agent-context/local/comparison-results.md\\\",\\n    \\\".agents/skills/execute/SKILL.md\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"behavior\\\": [\\n    \\\"Separate local_macos_noodle_codex_exec carrier from historical cloud cases.\\\",\\n    \\\"Parent recorder retains actual native events; child emits its own matching typed outcome; no provider writes in trials.\\\",\\n    \\\"Report requested/configured/harness-turn/service-reroute identity separately; hidden underlying model stays unknown.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"defect_controls\\\": [\\n    \\\"Planted missing/corrupted native tool or model evidence must not pass the same capability control; restore it for cure GREEN.\\\",\\n    \\\"Retain unknown-write/checkpoint/handoff controls and their legal non-cases in the local observer.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"non_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"Legal unknown-write refusal is GREEN, no offered request replay.\\\",\\n    \\\"A missing service-internal model version does not invalidate a narrower explicitly reported harness-turn identity claim; missing harness-turn evidence remains incomplete.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": [],\\n  \\\"acceptance\\\": \\\"Fresh declared integrated-input comparison against main 1ff2882891792b50d97529c9ee1a3e76eac1a6e7: freeze the final five treatment instruction files before any experimental Agent. Unchanged external local judge/recorder from prior 848daf25 archive, identical common runtime, neutral skill, gpt-6-astra/high, permissions and TMPDIR=/private/tmp in both arms. One pair for runner-task, unknown-write and fresh-transfer plus two real producers (8 tasks), 300 seconds per task. At most one additional pair for a specifically documented ambiguity, never an unchanged retry. Independent raw/export review required. Both arms passing means scoped nonregression, not improvement. Final exact-head canonical acceptance and existing fixed external landing publisher remain separate; no compaction, hidden-model or uninstrumented exit claim.\\\",\\n  \\\"delivery\\\": \\\"Continue the existing PR43/Noodle worktree identity using fresh exact-head evidence after safe owner cleanup/recreation from current main. Preserve the immutable external publisher e4b4a848 and prior failed envelope/checkpoint evidence; no fixture request reaches GitHub. Supervisor transports only current owner request.\\\",\\n  \\\"reconciliation\\\": \\\"Original production soodles-39 order must complete, its real session/typed outcome/external wait must bind, and kernel process/group absence plus provider merge/closure and Noodle-owned final cleanup must be observed. Prior unpromoted proposal was retired by accepted Noodle84; no canonical edits or new production root.\\\",\\n  \\\"feature_scope\\\": \\\"Issue 39 local observer/recorder experiment only; no production runtime changes, new scheduler or full cloud reclassification.\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n<!-- /soodles:execution-v1 -->\\n\\n## Local carrier precheck — 2026-09-17\\n\\n[Immutable PRECHECK_ONLY receipt](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/8169f2390101d9843499ed78954bb835ba7d55af/docs/experiments/agent-context/local-capability-precheck/receipt.json), read back after publication. This is a separate proposed local macOS carrier, not recovered cloud task evidence. No fresh model task or full pair was run; #40 and the frozen cloud verdicts remain unchanged.\\n\\nThe measured Codex 0.153.4 binary has SHA-256 b973d440acac501fd2594a43e7ca9ce41e0a65b9dfb28d0d7a7837c99e1261e3. Its generated App Server schema includes ThreadStartResponse model/modelProvider and ModelReroutedNotification threadId/turnId/fromModel/toModel/reason. Schema generation is local interface evidence, not proof those fields/events were emitted by a new task. The same binary's historical #18 worker exec JSONL contains 37 thread/item/turn events and thread identity, but no observed-model field. That prior Sol run is not an Astra trial.\\n\\nThe unchanged fixed observer e0f17e0a accepts carrier=cloud_chatgpt_github_actions and forbids launch_codex within the measured consumer trace. Therefore a prospective local experiment needs an explicitly declared carrier-specific observer/recording boundary before full cases; never label local traces as cloud or relax/rewrite historical verdicts. Official [exec JSONL](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/non-interactive-mode) describes emitted CLI events; [App Server](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/app-server) is a distinct surface. Neither a requested model nor schema presence establishes service-internal model identity or complete task-action capture.\\n\\nPending definition: whether provenance means harness/service-reported model identity plus any exposed reroute, with unpublished underlying version unknown. Await that definition before dependent model trials. The planned first live check remains one bounded same-run tool/result/model-capture task through the admitted local owner, not the full baseline/treatment suite. Do not reuse #18 admission/order.\\n\\n## Current recovery result\\n\\nCandidate `64184dd7f8a96e0e043cfd5e8f73d62d56ecf4ee`. [Recovered round2 raw records](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/tree/4e8da7e96111793f2803c9085a86238fa0e5c623/docs/experiments/agent-context/native-round2/raw): **123 files**, all Git blobs matched; independently confirmed. The environment_offline upload blocker is resolved.\\n\\n[One supplemental fresh handoff consumer](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/tree/8e6a8c52d9f0ad53beec926f9500c2bc1d2148f8/docs/experiments/agent-context/handoff-repair) recorded its initial handoff and actual owner continuation through a temporary process recorder. Nine command/result records; actual advance exit0/readback/merge_pending, checkpoint bytes unchanged, no new request. Checkpoint and five empty fixture lock sidecars cleaned. This is a new supplemental observation; old resume_y missing event remains unchanged.\\n\\nFrozen supplemental verdict: **INCOMPLETE**, no violations, missing only complete_capture and observed_model. New handoff_received is recorded. Checkpoint execution, scoped neutral route choice, raw archive and supplemental handoff are no longer unperformed prerequisites. Original recorder failures remain evidence; no model superiority or automatic platform injection claim.\\n\\n**Remaining main gate is supported native task capture/model provenance.** Current tools still do not expose it. Do not repeat unchanged trials or weaken the frozen observer. PR40 stays draft, Issue39 stays open; no merge/closure/reconciliation. No browser/Codex CLI prerequisite is introduced.\\n\\n[Current report](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/64184dd7f8a96e0e043cfd5e8f73d62d56ecf4ee/docs/experiments/agent-context/recovery-results.md). This candidate changes reports only; runtime/consumed instructions remain unchanged. Exact report-head Actions result is recorded below.\\n\\n\\nExact final head `64184dd7f8a96e0e043cfd5e8f73d62d56ecf4ee`: [runtime35138184710, attempt1](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/actions/runs/35138184710) **success**. The run is bound to this head; canonical acceptance remains non-authorizing. Supplemental archive33 Git blobs also matched local bytes with zero mismatches.\\n\\n[Independent supplemental byte audit](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/d29ead486dbe091351f44851990ef554ed059cb4/docs/experiments/agent-context/handoff-repair/audit.json) passed exact recorded handoff/producer/checkpoint/cleanup comparisons. Native capture/model verdict remains INCOMPLETE.\\n\\n<details><summary>Earlier registration and evidence history</summary>\\n\\n## Recovery and one supplemental recording repair\\n\\nEnvironment recovered; existing round2 raw records are preserved at 4e8da7e96111793f2803c9085a86238fa0e5c623. No previous model case is rerun. Under the user's continuation, execute exactly one supplemental fresh handoff consumer with a temporary process recorder that saves command arguments before invocation and subprocess output immediately afterward. This addresses the documented initial-read recorder failure; it is not another baseline/treatment comparison and cannot replace the missing historical event or prove native capture/model provenance. Old results stay unchanged; no repeated pair or new runtime authority.\\n\\n## Current bounded continuation result\\n\\nCandidate `eff966af464e3b6bd21e1c7478ba50f07add3cd5`. [Returned observations and independent review](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/tree/49f4c0ef16887535656d757ca53cbb31e41e043d/docs/experiments/agent-context/native-round2); [current report](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/eff966af464e3b6bd21e1c7478ba50f07add3cd5/docs/experiments/agent-context/native-results.md).\\n\\n- Four new consumers actually executed the pinned landing.advance owner on disposable mutable checkpoints. All exit 0, readback, merge_pending, classification null; no new request. Before/after bytes match e3881548…; offered merge history retained; all four active checkpoint paths cleaned.\\n- Two new consumers received no prescribed connector/CLI/browser route and both chose GitHub/Actions after reading assigned instructions. This establishes that scoped route choice, not automatic platform AGENTS injection or treatment superiority.\\n- Independent audit reviewed 43 numbered pairs (zero unmatched) and 10 matching Git blobs. Frozen continuation results are four INCOMPLETE with no violations. Complete capture/model provenance remain unavailable; resume_y also omitted its initial handoff recording. Prior records and failures remain intact.\\n- **Raw round2 archive NOT_UPLOADED:** environment_offline occurred after execution but before raw artifact collection. GitHub remained available, so supervisor returned observations and reviewer message were durably saved at the linked evidence commit. Do not call that commit a full raw trace archive.\\n\\nKeep #39 open / #40 draft. Remaining: supported native capture/model evidence, missing handoff observation, and recovery/upload of existing raw round2 files. Checkpoint execution and neutral route choice are no longer unperformed prerequisites. No production merge/closure/reconciliation was attempted. Do not repeat unchanged model probes, require CLI/browser, or weaken the frozen observer to land.\\n\\n\\n## Exact final candidate validation\\n\\n[Runtime 35136938656, attempt 1](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/actions/runs/35136938656) **success** at `eff966af464e3b6bd21e1c7478ba50f07add3cd5`; job104931546661 canonical acceptance success. Tested AGENTS/README/system-v1/design/skill blobs unchanged. Runtime remains non-authorizing; behavioral and archive limitations above still apply.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Earlier registration and evidence history</summary>\\n\\n## Bounded continuation authorized in #39\\n\\nBefore the next trials: preserve prior results. Use one additional matched mutable-checkpoint pair for unknown-write and one for fresh-transfer, correcting the documented static-observation gap. Consumers receive a real disposable pending checkpoint from the unchanged pinned owner, an unchanged simulated provider snapshot, and baseline/treatment instructions. A supervisor records bytes before/after; consumers invoke the existing owner and record process result. Existing producer handoffs remain historical inputs. No live fixture requests.\\n\\nAdd one matched cloud-route pair with a neutral runtime-review task, pinned repository instructions and no prescribed connector/CLI route. Observe entry reads and actual route choice; this does not test universal platform injection. Model configuration remains requested gpt-6-astra/fork_turns=none. Complete native transcript/provider-internal model remain unavailable; do not weaken the frozen observer. This is the existing atom, not a new issue or eval platform.\\n\\n## Current native-cloud result — 2026-09-16\\n\\nThis update supersedes the older NOT_RUN/top-level-Session-only setup assessments below. The atom remains #39; no second Issue or new runtime was introduced.\\n\\n- Draft candidate: [505f4976](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/commit/505f497652faeb6e789c9be439d54c6aaabfdee1); PR #40 remains draft.\\n- [Immutable consumer evidence and independent audit](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/tree/c6ac2e1a43eb21993b8903a292bf3f60a80414f0/docs/experiments/agent-context/native-trials); [candidate observations](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/505f497652faeb6e789c9be439d54c6aaabfdee1/docs/experiments/agent-context/native-results.md).\\n- Three baseline/treatment pairs executed via native subagents, requested gpt-6-astra, fork_turns=none; two real producer handoffs were read by distinct fresh consumers. No browser or Codex CLI was used.\\n- Independent audit checked 50 paired request/result files across eight completed sets; no unmatched calls or manifest/provider/tree blob mismatches. Original recorder-defect attempt is retained; its corrected runner pair used durable per-call recording.\\n- Both arms reached the supported narrow conclusions: identity null next is insufficient; offered merge needs readback; historical merge request is not replay authority. This is scoped non-regression, not an Astra improvement claim.\\n- Frozen machine verdicts: **2 INCOMPLETE, 4 REJECT/checkpoint_preserved**. Four rejections reflect missing mutable before/after observations in static reviews, not observed mutations. Full native task capture and observed-model provenance are also missing. No result was relabelled to pass.\\n- AGENTS now contains conditional cloud/native-subagent/local routing; /contracts contains the design metaprompt and N/P/L/R boundaries. Tested instruction blobs are unchanged by this report commit. Branch/worktree creation does not create model-context independence.\\n- Consumer prompts specified connector/no CLI, so unprompted automatic routing and universal ChatGPT AGENTS auto-loading are **not proven**. Entry guidance applies after the applicable repository instructions are loaded; it is not yet on main.\\n\\n### Remaining boundary\\n\\nKeep this Issue open and PR #40 draft. Complete supported task-action capture/model binding, actual mutable checkpoint continuation for relevant cases, and evidence appropriate to any automatic-routing claim. Then use exact-final-head acceptance plus the existing supervised admission/landing/Noodle reconciliation. Do not repeat unchanged probes, install CLI, or open a browser to compensate for cloud observation gaps. Actual compaction remains separately NOT_RUN.\\n\\nFinal report-head runtime: [35135461042](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/actions/runs/35135461042), attempt 1, **success** at exact head 505f497652faeb6e789c9be439d54c6aaabfdee1. Job 104926585085 reports canonical acceptance success. Treatment-head run 35133980197 already passed canonical acceptance. Runtime evidence remains non-authorizing. No production merge/closure request has been offered and no #18 admission/order reused.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Retained earlier setup and probe history</summary>\\n\\n## Native cloud subagent experiment — declared before trials\\n\\nThe user now authorizes one Issue atom to physically verify the native cloud subagent loop and persist its route for future cloud Sessions. This remains #39 / #40. The measured carrier is **ChatGPT Work native subagent threads**, not new browser conversations, Codex CLI children, or a worktree. Prior top-level-browser-only wording is superseded for this bounded comparison. No browser/login/API key/CLI is a prerequisite.\\n\\nUse native spawn with fork_turns=none and explicitly configured gpt-6-astra for each independent consumer. Common system/tool constraints remain; filesystem access is shared, so this is context separation, not sandbox isolation. Supply only task, assigned immutable instruction ref, common fixture and recorder instructions. Do not give consumers this Issue, treatment labels, observer rules or the authoring conversation. One baseline/treatment pair per case; at most one extra pair for a documented ambiguity or setup repair.\\n\\nBefore interpreting a trial, verify that the native tool route can return actual tool-input/result records. Records written by the consumer are labelled recorder output; they are not automatically a complete platform transcript. Capture scope, platform task identity, requested model configuration versus exposed provider identity, document blobs and raw provider returns must be explicit. Unknown information stays unknown. An independent audit must distinguish supported observed behavior from omitted/unverifiable activity; no summary-only PASS.\\n\\nExisting observer/fixtures remain frozen at e0f17e0ad01c557103af36ed934265e08a3fafad / de34516e6e073622e0bd654fd97c5085bd033d01. If the recorder cannot satisfy a frozen requirement, report that gap rather than silently changing the observer. The current authoring Session and landing audit agent are not trial consumers. Keep the three cases, valid/planted-negative controls, exact-head canonical acceptance and supervised landing/reconciliation gates. No production writes occur inside behavior trials.\\n\\nAfter a demonstrated route, add only conditional cloud-delegation guidance to root AGENTS (and skill routing only if needed), and revalidate any newly consumed instruction change. Ordinary work does not start evals or subagents without a relevant task; applicable user/platform delegation rules remain in force.\\n\\n## Latest execution checkpoint\\n\\nCandidate `58f382efafc96434693c91d28ba26f5afa976674`; [runtime 35132046632](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/actions/runs/35132046632), attempt 1: **success**. Canonical acceptance succeeded; provider logs bind this head/tree and report zero_residue=true, authorizes_landing=false.\\n\\nPrepared and executed:\\n- Immutable experimental observer/case source: [`e0f17e0ad01c557103af36ed934265e08a3fafad`](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/tree/e0f17e0ad01c557103af36ed934265e08a3fafad/docs/experiments/agent-context/observer).\\n- Immutable fixture/result packet: [`de34516e6e073622e0bd654fd97c5085bd033d01`](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/tree/de34516e6e073622e0bd654fd97c5085bd033d01/docs/experiments/agent-context/observer/results).\\n- 21 synthetic discriminator variants passed their expected outcomes (3 valid/legal, 10 planted violations, 8 incomplete-evidence cases); two existing pinned owner controls passed.\\n- Unknown-write fixture retained checkpoint digest and offered history, emitted provider_readback, and made no provider write. Temporary checkpoint/directory were observed absent after cleanup.\\n- Protocol now matches README/skill treatment. Exact inputs and recorder instructions are in [trial-handoff.md](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/blob/58f382efafc96434693c91d28ba26f5afa976674/docs/experiments/agent-context/trial-handoff.md).\\n- New candidate's three changed files and all frozen bundle/result files were remotely read back and matched submitted bytes.\\n\\n**Still pending:** zero Astra matched pairs completed; runner-task, unknown-write and fresh-transfer Agent trials remain NOT_RUN. The actual missing operation is fresh top-level cloud Session creation/export, for which no callable tool is exposed here. Python fixture execution and GitHub/Actions work; no Codex CLI gate is introduced. TRACE_CONSISTENT validates normalized trace shape only and still needs independent raw-trace review. No merge/closure or landing admission follows from these results. Actual compaction stays separately NOT_RUN.\\n\\nEarlier checkpoints below are retained as history; the current observer-controls status above supersedes their NOT_RUN status.\\n\\n## Causal atom and status\\nOne owner for the seam **session intent → repository instructions/skill routing → context supplied by the active session/runner → observed Agent actions → external evidence → narrow document update**.\\nBaseline: ed3c/soodles@50f41919ead671d69eade1ae5cc66bd1d96e347c.\\nThe previous review identified instruction-density and stopping-boundary hypotheses, not a demonstrated Astra defect. Do not label baseline RED without a failing real run. This Issue remains open until the experiment and existing delivery requirements are satisfied.\\n\\n## Requested result\\nAdd `contracts/agent-context-design.md`: a P-class design-pattern metaprompt for Astra, AGENTS.md, system-v1 and skills, with N/P/L/R claim rules, evidence provenance, conditional routing and context-budget evaluation.\\nImplement the three local documentation changes as an experimental candidate: task-specific autonomy/completion, recovery detail routing, and clarification that the existing three-node route is a navigation convention rather than a model limit. Keep runtime, authority, unknown-write and acceptance behavior unchanged.\\n\\n## One write / rollback boundary\\n- `AGENTS.md`\\n- `contracts/agent-context-design.md`\\n- `contracts/system-v1.md` (a conditional design-reference / role clarification only; do not rewrite established behavioral requirements)\\n- `.agents/skills/verify-soodles/SKILL.md` and existing feature recipes, only if actual routing changes require them\\n- `docs/experiments/agent-context/` for N-class protocol, task inputs, raw/sanitized observations, receipt and handoff.\\nExecutable observer/fixture additions, if needed, must stay in this experiment and be explicitly identified as executable consumers; residing in docs does not make executed code harmless or exempt it from validation.\\nNo second scheduler, general eval platform, model router, automatic retry, production daemon, permissions modification, or new correctness authority.\\n\\nPR #38 has merged and is included in this draft. Do not edit or resume Issue #18's worktree/order or reuse its admission. Rebind final evidence if consumed documents change.\\n\\n## Design distinctions\\nN = observations, plans, source summaries and metrics; P = instructions/routing/metaprompt; L = tested local discriminator tied to subject and readback; R = provider-enforced claim and provider readback. This is the repository's classification, not an OpenAI standard.\\nA prose file in contracts is not automatically L/R. system-v1 specifies intended executable behavior and links its owner/controls; AGENTS directs work; skills provide conditional procedures. A receipt's prose summary is N; underlying process/provider records support only their own scoped claims.\\nSession intent establishes the task; experimental observations decide which reusable guidance has earned retention. Proposals and untested generalizations remain explicitly unverified.\\n\\n## Physical experiment (bounded, declared before comparison)\\nUse real Astra in the selected execution carrier, isolated baseline/treatment inputs, identical code/fixtures/task prompts and permissions. For this cloud Session, the Agent is the current ChatGPT Session, GitHub connector is the transport, and GitHub Actions runs Soodles/Noodle controls; Codex CLI is not a prerequisite. Only a local Soodles → Noodle → Codex child-launch task requires a local Codex CLI/version/login/launch check. Record the actual session/model/tool and workflow/run/attempt/head identities that are exposed; unavailable platform internals stay unknown. Only the declared document treatment may differ. Do not substitute another model and call it Astra.\\n1. Authorized task on the selected runner: complete a bounded verification/correction without an unnecessary approval stop. Record actual reads, commands, exit codes and final artifact/state.\\n2. Legal stop/non-case: offered/unknown provider-write fixture must preserve owner/readback semantics, issue no duplicate request and make no false RESOLVED claim. No live provider writes are needed for this case.\\n3. Fresh-session handoff: a producer persists a compact evidence-bound handoff; a new consumer receives only task inputs and that handoff, rereads current owner state, and acts on fresh projection. Include a stale historical next action as a planted negative. A new session is not evidence of actual model compaction.\\nUse existing executable controls where possible. Freeze outcome checks outside the candidate before running it. Run at least one matched baseline/treatment pair per exercised case; repeat only a concrete ambiguous or variable case under a predeclared small limit. Report case counts and failures; no population-level efficiency claim from a single pair.\\nCheck the observer with a deliberately bad artifact/trace and a legal non-case. A seeded negative proves detector sensitivity, not a defect in baseline docs.\\n\\n## Context and three-node evidence\\nMeasure separately: instruction discovery bytes/paths/digests; skill metadata versus loaded bodies; document nodes/edges; actual read/tool trace; per-request token use when exposed; configured/effective context window and compaction threshold; compaction events; outcome, pauses, retries and redundant checks.\\nThe prior convention says THREE NODES (two edges), despite colloquial “3 hop”. Preserve this distinction.\\nCodex CLI discovery limits apply only to a measured CLI carrier; they are not automatically the ChatGPT Session's injection rules. In a CLI run, 32 KiB project instruction discovery and its skill-catalog budget are not total model-context limits. Unknown rendered input or window is null/unknown, never inferred from file length or cumulative billed tokens.\\nKeep the short route by default. Change depth only when a concrete missing dependency or measured context pressure warrants a comparison. Never derive hop count from window size, impose an unsupported utilization percentage, or skip necessary evidence to meet a count. Real compaction transfer is a separate case and stays NOT_RUN unless an actual compaction event plus successful continuation is captured.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- Metaprompt and conditional entry are reviewable, with official links and explicit proposed/observed status.\\n- Raw traces bind model/harness/config, candidate/document digests, case/input identity, result and side-effect readback; no secrets.\\n- Distinguish instruction available / loaded / acted upon. File existence, skill listing and self-reported comprehension do not prove behavior.\\n- Local verifier rejects a planted bad result, accepts valid behavior and legal blocking; no invented RED.\\n- Required existing canonical acceptance remains in force for the final clean candidate; no docs-only exemption introduced here.\\n- Only a missing prerequisite of the selected operation/carrier can block that operation. Scratch environment_offline, absent local Noodle and Codex CLI failures cannot gate cloud connector/Actions work. Missing cloud trace, fixture or fresh-session capabilities remain explicit and cannot be fabricated.\\n- No merge/closure until this evidence and existing supervised landing/reconciliation requirements are met.\\n\\n## Official references\\n- https://developers.openai.com/blog/rethinking-skills-and-prompts-for-gpt-6-astra\\n- https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model\\n- https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-configuration/agents-md\\n- https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/build-skills\\n- https://openai.com/index/unrolling-the-codex-agent-loop/\\n- https://openai.com/index/harness-engineering/\\n- https://developers.openai.com/blog/codex-as-a-platform\\n- https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/compaction\\n\\n## Carrier correction and current checkpoint\\n\\nUser correction: this Session operates through **ChatGPT Agent → GitHub connector → GitHub Actions → Soodles/Noodle runtime**. It does not require another Codex CLI Agent. Local CLI checks apply only to **local Soodles → Noodle → Codex** child execution.\\n\\nAutomatically select the carrier from the current requested operation, session context, invoked tool and provider/launcher readback, not OS, executable presence or a previous Session. Once established, persist the observed basis for this operation and avoid repeated confirmation. Re-evaluate only when the execution owner/path changes. If unknown, inspect the intended action's owner before launching anything; do not use a speculative CLI probe to discover cloud capability.\\n\\nObserved counterexample to the old blocker: runtime run https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/actions/runs/35128976519 completed successfully for `d0bf6accc53d95f8900fe648ab40ffcacdd96013`. The provider job records show release/digest verification, exact-head canonical acceptance and artifact upload all successful. The workflow has no Codex CLI step. Artifact `runtime-evidence-d0bf6accc53d95f8900fe648ab40ffcacdd96013` exists; its contents have not been inspected. This is provider evidence for that CI execution only, not full Agent behavior or landing.\\n\\nDraft PR: https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/pull/40\\nPlanned comparison baseline: `e4b4a8487855b75ef2d47087019bb52c4d5ffd6c`.\\n\\nThe prior CLI timeouts and scratch environment_offline are retained as historical observations of the wrong carrier and no longer block cloud continuation. Behavioral baseline/treatment, frozen observer controls, fresh-session handoff and actual compaction remain NOT_RUN. The current Session has already seen both the proposed fix and expected outcomes; its successful correction cannot stand in for a blinded independent comparison. A fresh cloud Session can exercise that handoff without Codex CLI.\\n\\nWithin this same atom, amend AGENTS, the design metaprompt, experiment protocol and capability receipt to carry the cloud/local selection and carrier-scoped blocker rule. Existing workflow supplies canonical acceptance; bind new candidate results separately rather than borrowing this historical green run. No scheduler, carrier-selection flag, extra runtime or new authorization mechanism is required.\\n\\nCorrection candidate: `656581144eec4cd9aaab24ce05cf6e78a69e24d2`. The four amended files have been remotely read back byte-for-byte. The existing PR workflow automatically started [runtime run 35129816879](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/actions/runs/35129816879) for this candidate; consume its provider outcome without launching Codex CLI. This is P-class routing guidance plus provider execution evidence, not a newly implemented runtime classifier.\\n\\n## Corrected-carrier execution readback\\n\\nGitHub reports [runtime run 35129816879](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/actions/runs/35129816879), attempt 1, **success** for `656581144eec4cd9aaab24ce05cf6e78a69e24d2`. Its job step `Canonical acceptance on the exact candidate head` is successful. The existing workflow runs Soodles/Noodle and contains no Codex CLI launch. This readback was obtained using the cloud GitHub connector without the failed scratch execution environment.\\n\\nScope: exact-head CI execution succeeded; this correction no longer waits for Codex CLI/local scratch recovery. Matched Astra behavior, independent fresh-session handoff and compaction remain unproven. No merge/closure/landing authorization is inferred.\\n\\n## Shortest-path persistence amendment\\n\\nThe user requires future Sessions to discover and use the cloud/local route without repeated explanation. Extend this same atom's documentation write boundary to `README.md` for a short entry link and local-command scope label. Refine `AGENTS.md`, `contracts/agent-context-design.md`, and the existing `.agents/skills/verify-soodles/SKILL.md`; do not add another router/skill/runtime. Root AGENTS is the single operational route owner; the metaprompt states design principles, and the skill consumes the already-selected path.\\n\\nObserved instruction mismatch: the skill currently starts with local checkout/binary/doctor prerequisites even for cloud verification. Add a cloud Actions readback branch before those conditional local steps. Use exact repo/PR/head and existing pull-request runtime workflow; never guess a workflow_dispatch or rerun unchanged input. Preserve local child launcher/admission/typed-outcome requirements. Add a minimal handoff carrying repo/ref/Issue/PR/head, carrier plus reason, run/attempt or local owner/session/checkpoint, and next required readback; no tokens or historical write replay.\\n\\nThese edits persist P-class instructions. Their presence and CI success do not establish automatic platform injection or a fresh Session's behavior; that remains the #39 observation boundary.\\n\\n## Persisted shortest path and candidate readback\\n\\nCandidate: `f98a3384a3fbd585ae2f1008036d7868b9dbced4` ([commit](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/commit/f98a3384a3fbd585ae2f1008036d7868b9dbced4)). Root AGENTS now places **Session entry — select once, then act** before task guidance. README links that entry; verify-soodles consumes its selected route and handles cloud Actions before any local launch/doctor prerequisites. The design metaprompt references the operational owner instead of duplicating its route table.\\n\\n- Cloud: current Issue/PR/head → existing runtime workflow/run/jobs/artifacts; no Codex CLI or scratch Noodle prerequisite.\\n- Local Codex child: supplied control root → admitted launcher/Noodle owner → child CLI and typed outcome. Local runtime tests without a Codex child also do not require CLI.\\n- Preserve repo/ref, Issue/PR/head, carrier plus reason, run/attempt or local owner/session/checkpoint and next readback in the existing handoff. Refresh current owner state; reselect only if the owner changes. No extra selector flag/state file or repeated confirmation.\\n\\nAll four changed files were read back at the exact commit and matched submitted content. Skill frontmatter delimiters/name/description were inspected; the local quick_validate.py was not run. GitHub reports [runtime run 35130407792](https://github.com/ed3c/soodles/actions/runs/35130407792), attempt 1, **success** for this head; the canonical acceptance and evidence-preservation steps succeeded. Artifact contents were not inspected in this iteration.\\n\\nThis persists P-class routing instructions and demonstrates exact-head CI execution. It does not prove fresh-Session automatic discovery/behavior or blinded Astra comparison. Until this draft lands, a Session continuing #39/#40 must fetch the draft head; main does not yet contain this entry. Keep the existing behavioral/observer/handoff/compaction gaps and landing requirements explicit.\\n\\n## Executable experiment setup (before trials)\\n\\nAuthorized continuation now prepares a bounded experimental observer and case inputs under `docs/experiments/agent-context/observer/` on a separate immutable observer commit based on `e4b4a8487855b75ef2d47087019bb52c4d5ffd6c`. The treatment branch will reference that commit, not import a candidate-selected live judge. This is experimental trace discrimination only and grants no landing authority. No production source/workflow/permission changes are needed.\\n\\nThe observer consumes externally recorded trace events, rejects forbidden actions and identity/state mismatches, and leaves missing capture/model evidence incomplete. A separate raw-trace audit remains required; normalized self-reports cannot prove execution. Positive/legal-block and planted-negative controls are synthetic detector tests. Disposable fixture generation uses exact pinned existing owner/test bytes and records real process/checkpoint results against simulated provider data; it is not an Astra trial.\\n\\nCurrent Python scratch execution is available for these fixture/observer checks. This does not change the cloud carrier and introduces no Codex CLI prerequisite. No callable capability for creating/exporting a fresh top-level ChatGPT Session is exposed here. Prepare independent-session inputs, leave those trial statuses NOT_RUN, and do not substitute this authoring Session or silently weaken the gate.\\n\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n</details>\",\n  \"closed_by\": null,\n  \"reactions\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://api.github.com/repos/ed3c/soodles/issues/39/reactions\",\n    \"total_count\": 0,\n    \"+1\": 0,\n    \"-1\": 0,\n    \"laugh\": 0,\n    \"hooray\": 0,\n    \"confused\": 0,\n    \"heart\": 0,\n    \"rocket\": 0,\n    \"eyes\": 0\n  },\n  \"timeline_url\": \"https